<Base title="Community guidelines draft" description="Draft community rules for Brick Legends. They are not in force." section="legends">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Draft · not in force</p>
    <h1 class="lede">Community guidelines</h1>
    <p>These notes describe the rules a later public gallery would use. They are not a terms-of-service agreement, and no public submission is open.</p>
    <h2>Original work</h2>
    <p>Characters must be the creator’s own designs. Do not upload another person’s art, a LEGO Group logo, a minifigure of a protected character, or someone else’s name as if it were yours.</p>
    <h2>Conduct</h2>
    <p>No harassment, sexual content involving minors, or instructions for harm. A published card can be reported. Reports are limited to ten a day for each account. The queue is not staffed until a moderator is appointed in the database.</p>
    <h2>Publication</h2>
    <p>A private draft can later be submitted. Submission does not mean the card is public. A reviewer would approve, reject, or remove it. Creators cannot approve themselves, assign awards, or change a vote total.</p>
    <h2>Commercial use</h2>
    <p>Publishing a digital card would not license it for a physical card or an auction. That permission is a separate consent, and no consent terms are published. The Annual Five is not open.</p>
    <h2>Quotas</h2>
    <p>Character creation is free. An account may store 200 characters. The record is the structured studio data, not a PNG for every private draft. Public artwork files stay closed. These limits are abuse controls, not a paid plan.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
